{
  "email": "ryan.brooks@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: confirm status of former employee account reported with failed logins (read-only)"
}

{
  "user_id": 10,
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check 2: review sign-in attempts on disabled former-employee account for security escalation"
}

{
  "summary": "P1 security, KB-005. Reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, verified sender). She is seeing failed-login alerts on former employee Ryan Brooks' account (user_id 10, Sales AE, left spring 2026). Findings: account status is 'disabled', but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true, so VPN access was not revoked at offboarding. Sign-in logs show 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 New York time), from Amsterdam, NL, IP 192.0.2.140, hosting network, no MFA. This looks like someone trying stolen or stuffed credentials. Password last set 2026-03-23. Device on record: BL-LT-0110 (check whether it was returned). Nothing changed by Tier 1: the account isn't the sender's, and KB-005 says not to reset or unlock. Still needed: security review, confirm sign-in block and VPN revocation on user_id 10, block or watch IP 192.0.2.140, check for other attempts from that IP against other accounts, and check the offboarding gap.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate. P1 security, with hosting-network VPN attempts on a disabled account that still has VPN access."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for flagging this, Priya. You were right to check. Ryan's account is disabled, but his VPN access was never turned off. There were two failed VPN sign-ins on it early this morning (about 3:05 and 3:07 a.m. Eastern) from a hosting network in Amsterdam. Both used the wrong password, so nobody got in. I didn't change anything on his account, because that's outside what the front-line help desk is allowed to do. I've sent it to our Tier 2 security team as urgent with everything I found, and they'll review it and lock down the remaining access.",
  "internal_note": "KB-005, P1. Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, uid 3), verified. Target: Ryan Brooks (uid 10), former employee. Status is disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true (an offboarding gap). Two failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC from Amsterdam, NL, IP 192.0.2.140, hosting network, no MFA. Neither succeeded. I took no action: the account isn't the sender's, and KB-005 says no reset or unlock. I didn't queue block_sign_in because it isn't the sender's account; Tier 2 should apply it and revoke VPN. Escalation id 1. Also check whether device BL-LT-0110 was returned and whether the IP is hitting other accounts.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
